      "text": "Given the operation \\( a \\nabla b = \\frac{a + b}{1 + ab} \\), we need to calculate \\( 2 \\nabla 5 \\).\n\nFirst, substitute \\( a = 2 \\) and \\( b = 5 \\) into the formula:\n\n\\[\n2 \\nabla 5 = \\frac{2 + 5}{1 + 2 \\times 5}\n\\]\n\nNext, perform the addition and multiplication in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n2 + 5 = 7\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\times 5 = 10\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n2 \\nabla 5 = \\frac{7}{1 + 10}\n\\]\n\nNow, perform the addition in the denominator:\n\n\\[\n1 + 10 = 11\n\\]\n\nSo the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n2 \\nabla 5 = \\frac{7}{11}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{11}}\n\\]",
